# "If that creature would die this turn, exile it instead" (CR 611.2c, 614.1a): the replacement lasts only until the turn
# ends (CR 514.2). Bot1's Ornithopter is the target of a Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn! with X = 0 on turn 1 - no damage, only the
# replacement - and on turn 5 a Fatal Push kills it: it goes to the graveyard, the replacement long gone. On turn 3 the
# same spell targets a creature, resolves, and a Fatal Push in the same turn kills it: it is exiled, so the death from
# another source is replaced and the graveyard never gets it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!
Fatal Push
Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!
Fatal Push
Swamp x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!.Cast(Ornithopter; X: 0)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves; X: 0)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Fatal Push.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Fatal Push.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves = (absent)
Exile = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Fatal Push; Ornithopter; Fatal Push; Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!; Khaaaaaaaaaaaannn!
